$ cessna210_flagship_body_strip_drv.bdf — SOL 144 trim with DECOUPLED STRIP
$ body panels (Step 66).
$
$ The controlled contrast to cessna210_flagship_body.bdf.  Identical airplane,
$ identical body-panel geometry, identical total-aircraft targets — the ONLY
$ difference is which overlay is INCLUDEd, i.e. whether the body boxes carry
$ PAERO1 (cruciform, AIC-coupled) or PSTRIP (strip, decoupled).
$
$ That single-variable design is the point.  A PSTRIP block of the influence
$ operator is diagonal, so under this deck the wing/HTP/VTP box loads come out
$ BIT-IDENTICAL to the bare flagship; under the cruciform they do not.  Running
$ both is the cheapest demonstration of what body-panel interference actually
$ costs, with everything else held fixed.
$
$ One subcase only — the cruciform deck carries the 2.5g case, and the contrast
$ this deck exists for is fully visible at 1g.
$
$ Walk-through: docs/20_theory/02_realistic_airplane_sol144.md section 8
$ Units: SI (m, N, kg, Pa, s)
$
SOL 144
TITLE = Cessna 210 flagship — decoupled strip body panels, 1g
INCLUDE 'cessna210_flagship_bulk.bdf'
INCLUDE 'cessna210_flagship_body_strip.bdf'
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE = 1g cruise with strip body panels, q = 2334 Pa
  TRIM  = 1
  SPC   = 1
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
  FORCE        = ALL
$
BEGIN BULK
ENDDATA
